Original work
  Everything else in this folder was written for this site in 2026: the
  circuit simulator (modified nodal analysis, Newton-Raphson, the
  transient engine and every device model), the sketch compiler and
  runtime, the part definitions, the procedural 3D models and material
  patterns, the 5 x 7 LCD font, the instruments, the panels, the 32
  example benches and the screensaver director. No code was ported from
  tutorial, shader or simulator sites.

Names and marks
  The microcontroller boards are generic: the models carry plain
  silkscreen pin names ("328 DEV BOARD", "WIFI DEVKIT") and no logos or
  trademark names. Part numbers (555, LM358, 74HC595, CD4017, 1N4148,
  2N3904 and so on) name the generic, multi-source devices whose
  datasheet behaviour the models follow.

Idea
  The page grew from the owner's earlier 2D "breadboard bench"
  (breadboard-designer-3.html), whose JSON benches the FILE panel can
  import.
